% Every predicate standing above a negative cycle depends on it, but only one
% on the cycle may be named.  Here the cycle is a <-> b, and c, d and e only
% negate their way down to it: the diagnostic names a, the first predicate
% with a negative edge that leads back to itself, and not one above it.
node(1).
a(X) :- node(X), not b(X).
b(X) :- node(X), not a(X).
c(X) :- node(X), not b(X).
d(X) :- node(X), not c(X).
e(X) :- node(X), not d(X).
